us to handle  manually especially when one is in a  hurry to quickly stop metabolism  these cold liquids are also incredibly  hard to handle and store  on an automated robotic system which  prevents automation of the workflow  after metabolism is quenched the  molecular components of the cells such  as proteins  metabolites and lipids are extracted  and for multi-omics analyses different  fractions of the cells are separated  for more facile analysis via lcms  this fractionation is commonly  accomplished via liquid liquid  separations  where polar metabolites favor an aqueous  phase proteins precipitate out  and lipids favor an organic phase  although effective  liquid liquid extractions are very  tricky to precisely separate  both manually and when automated  to overcome the challenges of cold  liquid metabolism quenching  we have developed a room temperature  method for lysine mammalian cells and  quickly quenching metabolism  using trifluoroethanol this room  temperature quenching method improves  workflow safety  reduces workflow complexity and enables  easy handling  of the quenching solution by automated  liquid handlers  to overcome the difficulty of separating  the liquid layers of liquid liquid  separations we have developed a solid  phase  extraction method this extraction method  utilizes the captiva emr lipid plate to  separate polar metabolites and lipids  for downstream  intra-sample multi-omics analyses it is  possible to automate these solid phase  extraction workflow steps  on the bravo liquid handler  this diagram outlines the first major  component of the new  dual metabolite plus lipid cell sample  prep workflow  cell lysis and metabolism quenching  initially  cells must be removed from the media in  which they are growing to isolate  intracellular metabolites  after media removal the cells can  optionally be washed with buffers like  pbs  to further remove extracellular  metabolites  since cell washing can cause leakage of  some metabolites  and